    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane through the point (2, 4, -3)
which is parallel to the plane <m>-1x  - 3y + 3z = 2</m> in
which the coefficient of x is -1.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1\mathopen{}\left(x-2\right)+\left(-3\right)\mathopen{}\left(y-4\right)+3\mathopen{}\left(z-\left(-3\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
